  keywords    = $q$Ionoelastomers, Polyelectrolyte Complexes, Iontronics & Electro-adhesion, Sustainable Polymer Chemistry$q$,
  bio_ko      = $q$<h3>학력</h3><ul><li>KAIST 생명화학공학과 2011 공학사</li><li>KAIST 생명화학공학과 2017 공학박사</li></ul><h3>경력</h3><ul><li>University of Massachusetts Amherst, Polymer Science and Engineering 박사후연구원 (2017–2020)</li><li>서강대학교 화공생명공학과 조교수 (2021–2025)</li><li>서강대학교 화공생명공학과 부교수 (2025–현재)</li></ul><h3>주요 수상</h3><ul><li>서강 알바트로스 학술상 (2026)</li><li>한국고분자학회 신진학술상 (2023)</li><li>서강 리치 공학 영펠로우 (2023)</li><li>서강 리치 공학 강의상 (2021)</li><li>Frank J. Padden Jr. Award Finalist, 미국물리학회 고분자물리분과 (2017)</li></ul><h3>학회 활동</h3><ul><li>한국고분자학회 운영위원 (2023–2025)</li><li>한국고분자학회 기술지 편집위원 (2022–2024)</li><li>한국화학공학회 고분자부문위원회 편집간사 (2023)</li></ul><h3>주요 논문</h3><ul><li>Younghoon Kim, Chankyu Kim, Seungju Lee, Chan-Hyuk Jeon, Han Hee Cho*, and Hyeong Jun Kim*, "<a href="https://doi.org/10.1021/acs.nanolett.6c02638">Kinetically Arrested Interfacial Polyelectrolyte Complexes Enable Ionic Rectification in Ionoelastomer Heterojunctions</a>," <em>Nano Letters</em> 26, 12725-12733 (2026)</li><li>Chankyu Kim†, Chan-Hyuk Jeon†, Jowon Shin, Younghoon Kim, Owen A. Lee, Ryan C. Hayward, and Hyeong Jun Kim*, "Electrically Induced Glass Transition in Polyelectrolyte Complexes Enables Kinetic Ionic Diodes," <em>Nature Communications</em> accepted (2026)</li><li>Yongsu Kim, Youngwon Lee, Ji Hee Yun, Noh-Moon Lee, Bonjae Koo, Jonggeol Na*, and Hyeong Jun Kim*, "<a href="https://www.nature.com/articles/s41467-026-76086-2">Recoverable Macroporous Polyanion Bead Catalysts for Scalable Continuous Chemical Depolymerization of Poly(Ethylene Terephthalate)</a>," <em>Nature Communications</em> 17, 9204 (2026)</li><li>Heewoon Shin, Owen A. Lee, Younghoon Kim, Ryan C. Hayward*, and Hyeong Jun Kim*, "<a href="https://pubs.acs.org/doi/10.1021/acselectrochem.5c00363">Effects of Network Elasticity on Asymmetric EDL Capacitance-Voltage Responses of Ionoelastomers</a>," <em>ACS Electrochemistry</em> 2, 146−153 (2026)</li><li>Yoon-Je Choi, Seungju Lee, Younghoon Kim, Sehwan Park, and Hyeong Jun Kim*, "<a href="https://advanced.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1002/advs.202510512">High Performance Electrochemical Adhesives Enabled by Perfluorinated Sulfonic-Acid Ionomers with Precise Adhesion Control and Long-Term Switchability</a>," <em>Advanced Science</em> e10512 (2025)</li><li>Jinseok Park†, Heewoon Shin†, Wonho Lee, Sheng Li, Hyeong Jun Kim*, and Bumjoon J. Kim*, "<a href="https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0079670025000231">Elastomeric Polymer Networks Electrolyte: Synthesis, Properties and Applications</a>," <em>Progress in Polymer Science</em> 163, 101944 (2025)</li><li>Jowon Shin, Heewoon Shin, Sang-Ho Lee, Jong Dae Jang, and Hyeong Jun Kim*, "<a href="https://pubs.acs.org/doi/10.1021/acsmacrolett.4c00663">Influence of Solvent Dielectric Constant on the Complex Coacervation Phase Behavior of Polymerized Ionic Liquids (PILs)</a>," <em>ACS Macro Letters</em> 13, 12, 1678-1685 (2024)</li><li>Sehwan Park, Yoon-Je Choi, Soonyong So and Hyeong Jun Kim*, "<a href="https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1002/adfm.202409443">Electrostatic Clutches Based on Ionomer Heterojunctions for Low-Voltage Switching of Stiffness and Strength</a>," <em>Advanced Functional Materials</em> 2409443 (2024)</li><li>D. J. Levine, O. A. Lee, G. M. Campbell, M. K. McBride, Hyeong Jun Kim, K. T. Turner, R. C. Hayward*, J. H. Pikul*, "<a href="https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1002/adma.202304455">A Low-Voltage, High-Force Capacity Electroadhesive Clutch Based on Ionoelastomer Heterojunctions</a>," <em>Advanced Materials</em> 35, 2304455 (2023)</li><li>Heewoon Shin, Jowon Shin, Ryan C. Hayward, and Hyeong Jun Kim*, "<a href="https://pubs.acs.org/doi/full/10.1021/acs.macromol.3c01092">Ionoelastomers at Electrified Interfaces: Differential Electric Double Layer Capacitances of Crosslinked Polymeric Ions and Mobile Counter Ions</a>," <em>Macromolecules</em> 56, 19, 7827-7836 (2023)</li><li>Yecheng Wang, Kun Jia, Shuwen Zhang, Hyeong Jun Kim, Yang Bai, Ryan C. Hayward, and Zhigang Suo*, "<a href="https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.2117962119">Temperature Sensing Using Junctions Between Mobile Ions and Mobile Electrons</a>," <em>PNAS</em> 119, 4, e2117962119 (2022)</li><li>Hyeong Jun Kim, Lindsay Paquin, Christopher W. Barney, Soonyong So, Baohong Chen, Zhigang Suo*, Alfred J. Crosby*, and Ryan C. Hayward*, "<a href="https://doi.org/10.1002/adma.202000600">Low-Voltage Reversible Electro-Adhesion of Ionoelastomer Junctions</a>," <em>Advanced Materials</em> 2000600 (2020)</li><li>Hyeong Jun Kim, Baohong Chen, Zhigang Suo*, and Ryan C. Hayward*, "<a href="https://doi.org/10.1126/science.aay8467">Ionoelastomer Junctions Between Polymer Networks of Fixed Anions and Cations</a>," <em>Science</em> 367, 773 (2020)</li></ul>$q$,
  bio_en      = $q$<h3>Education</h3><ul><li>B.S., Chemical and Biomolecular Engineering, KAIST (2011)</li><li>Ph.D., Chemical and Biomolecular Engineering, KAIST (2017)</li></ul><h3>Experience</h3><ul><li>Postdoctoral Researcher, Polymer Science and Engineering, University of Massachusetts Amherst (2017–2020)</li><li>Assistant Professor, Chemical and Biomolecular Engineering, Sogang University (2021–2025)</li><li>Associate Professor, Chemical and Biomolecular Engineering, Sogang University (2025–present)</li></ul><h3>Selected Awards</h3><ul><li>Sogang Albatross Academic Award (2026)</li><li>Young Scholar Award, The Polymer Society of Korea (2023)</li><li>Sogang Ricci Engineering Young Fellow (2023)</li><li>Sogang Ricci Excellence in Teaching Award (2021)</li><li>Frank J. Padden Jr. Award Finalist, Division of Polymer Physics, APS (2017)</li></ul><h3>Professional Service</h3><ul><li>The Polymer Society of Korea, Steering Committee (2023–2025)</li><li>The Polymer Society of Korea, Editorial Board (2022–2024)</li><li>The Korean Institute of Chemical Engineers, Polymer Division Editorial Secretary (2023)</li></ul><h3>Selected Publications</h3><ul><li>Younghoon Kim, Chankyu Kim, Seungju Lee, Chan-Hyuk Jeon, Han Hee Cho*, and Hyeong Jun Kim*, "<a href="https://doi.org/10.1021/acs.nanolett.6c02638">Kinetically Arrested Interfacial Polyelectrolyte Complexes Enable Ionic Rectification in Ionoelastomer Heterojunctions</a>," <em>Nano Letters</em> 26, 12725-12733 (2026)</li><li>Chankyu Kim†, Chan-Hyuk Jeon†, Jowon Shin, Younghoon Kim, Owen A. Lee, Ryan C. Hayward, and Hyeong Jun Kim*, "Electrically Induced Glass Transition in Polyelectrolyte Complexes Enables Kinetic Ionic Diodes," <em>Nature Communications</em> accepted (2026)</li><li>Yongsu Kim, Youngwon Lee, Ji Hee Yun, Noh-Moon Lee, Bonjae Koo, Jonggeol Na*, and Hyeong Jun Kim*, "<a href="https://www.nature.com/articles/s41467-026-76086-2">Recoverable Macroporous Polyanion Bead Catalysts for Scalable Continuous Chemical Depolymerization of Poly(Ethylene Terephthalate)</a>," <em>Nature Communications</em> 17, 9204 (2026)</li><li>Heewoon Shin, Owen A. Lee, Younghoon Kim, Ryan C. Hayward*, and Hyeong Jun Kim*, "<a href="https://pubs.acs.org/doi/10.1021/acselectrochem.5c00363">Effects of Network Elasticity on Asymmetric EDL Capacitance-Voltage Responses of Ionoelastomers</a>," <em>ACS Electrochemistry</em> 2, 146−153 (2026)</li><li>Yoon-Je Choi, Seungju Lee, Younghoon Kim, Sehwan Park, and Hyeong Jun Kim*, "<a href="https://advanced.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1002/advs.202510512">High Performance Electrochemical Adhesives Enabled by Perfluorinated Sulfonic-Acid Ionomers with Precise Adhesion Control and Long-Term Switchability</a>," <em>Advanced Science</em> e10512 (2025)</li><li>Jinseok Park†, Heewoon Shin†, Wonho Lee, Sheng Li, Hyeong Jun Kim*, and Bumjoon J. Kim*, "<a href="https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0079670025000231">Elastomeric Polymer Networks Electrolyte: Synthesis, Properties and Applications</a>," <em>Progress in Polymer Science</em> 163, 101944 (2025)</li><li>Jowon Shin, Heewoon Shin, Sang-Ho Lee, Jong Dae Jang, and Hyeong Jun Kim*, "<a href="https://pubs.acs.org/doi/10.1021/acsmacrolett.4c00663">Influence of Solvent Dielectric Constant on the Complex Coacervation Phase Behavior of Polymerized Ionic Liquids (PILs)</a>," <em>ACS Macro Letters</em> 13, 12, 1678-1685 (2024)</li><li>Sehwan Park, Yoon-Je Choi, Soonyong So and Hyeong Jun Kim*, "<a href="https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1002/adfm.202409443">Electrostatic Clutches Based on Ionomer Heterojunctions for Low-Voltage Switching of Stiffness and Strength</a>," <em>Advanced Functional Materials</em> 2409443 (2024)</li><li>D. J. Levine, O. A. Lee, G. M. Campbell, M. K. McBride, Hyeong Jun Kim, K. T. Turner, R. C. Hayward*, J. H. Pikul*, "<a href="https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1002/adma.202304455">A Low-Voltage, High-Force Capacity Electroadhesive Clutch Based on Ionoelastomer Heterojunctions</a>," <em>Advanced Materials</em> 35, 2304455 (2023)</li><li>Heewoon Shin, Jowon Shin, Ryan C. Hayward, and Hyeong Jun Kim*, "<a href="https://pubs.acs.org/doi/full/10.1021/acs.macromol.3c01092">Ionoelastomers at Electrified Interfaces: Differential Electric Double Layer Capacitances of Crosslinked Polymeric Ions and Mobile Counter Ions</a>," <em>Macromolecules</em> 56, 19, 7827-7836 (2023)</li><li>Yecheng Wang, Kun Jia, Shuwen Zhang, Hyeong Jun Kim, Yang Bai, Ryan C. Hayward, and Zhigang Suo*, "<a href="https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.2117962119">Temperature Sensing Using Junctions Between Mobile Ions and Mobile Electrons</a>," <em>PNAS</em> 119, 4, e2117962119 (2022)</li><li>Hyeong Jun Kim, Lindsay Paquin, Christopher W. Barney, Soonyong So, Baohong Chen, Zhigang Suo*, Alfred J. Crosby*, and Ryan C. Hayward*, "<a href="https://doi.org/10.1002/adma.202000600">Low-Voltage Reversible Electro-Adhesion of Ionoelastomer Junctions</a>," <em>Advanced Materials</em> 2000600 (2020)</li><li>Hyeong Jun Kim, Baohong Chen, Zhigang Suo*, and Ryan C. Hayward*, "<a href="https://doi.org/10.1126/science.aay8467">Ionoelastomer Junctions Between Polymer Networks of Fixed Anions and Cations</a>," <em>Science</em> 367, 773 (2020)</li></ul>$q$,
  research_ko = $q$<p>하전 고분자는 생체 고분자부터 첨단 기술의 합성 고분자 전해질까지 어디에나 있습니다. 고분자 이온 소재 연구실은 하전 고분자의 물리화학적 현상을 이해하고, 이를 부드럽고 크게 변형되는 기능성 소자로 옮기는 연구를 합니다.</p><p>이온성 고분자 설계와 합성<br>고분자 전해질과 고분자화 이온성 액체를 주사슬 구조, 전하 밀도, 짝이온을 조절하며 합성하고, 화학 가교·물리적 결합·이중 네트워크·중합 유도 상분리를 이용해 탄성 네트워크로 만듭니다. 이온이 네트워크에 고정되어 있어 늘어나는 동시에 이온을 전도하는 소재가 됩니다. 가교 밀도, 이온 함량, 염 도핑이 강성과 유전 특성, 그리고 전극 계면에 저장되는 전하량을 어떻게 결정하는지 연구합니다.</p><p>복합 코아세르베이션과 상거동<br>반대 전하를 띤 고분자 전해질을 섞으면 회합성 상분리가 일어나 농후한 복합체 상과 묽은 상으로 나뉩니다. 전하 밀도, 염, 용매에 따라 상경계가 어디에 놓이는지 정량적으로 밝히고, 이를 농후상의 구조와 역학 물성에 연결합니다. 농후상은 단순한 액체가 아닙니다. 물과 염이 가소제로 작용해 유리전이를 조절할 수 있고, 전기장으로 유리전이를 유도할 수도 있습니다. 이를 통해 복합체 안에서 이온이 움직이는 속도와 계면에서 형성된 복합체의 거동을 제어합니다.</p><p>소프트 이온 소자, 이온트로닉스, 전기접착<br>고정 음이온 네트워크와 고정 양이온 네트워크가 만나면 이동 짝이온이 재배열되어 접합부에 이온 이중층이 형성됩니다. 이 층은 수 볼트에 반응하므로, 배터리 수준의 전압으로 강하고 가역적인 접착이 가능해집니다. 이중층의 형성과 방전, 네트워크 탄성이 정전용량-전압 응답에 미치는 영향, 같은 접합이 이온 전류를 정류하는 원리를 연구하고, 이를 전기접착 클러치, 그리퍼, 로봇 엔드이펙터처럼 강성과 파지력을 필요할 때 전환하는 소자로 구현합니다.</p><p>지속가능 고분자 화학<br>대부분의 고분자는 만들기보다 분해하기가 훨씬 어렵습니다. 폐쇄 순환형 화학적 재활용을 위해 해중합을 연구하며, 어떤 결합이 온화한 조건에서 다시 열리는지, 고분자 구조가 깨끗한 단량체 회수를 어떻게 좌우하는지 묻습니다. 촉매로는 거대 기공 폴리음이온 비드를 사용합니다. 활성점이 고체 지지체에 고정되어 있어 촉매를 걸러 다시 쓸 수 있고, 연속 공정과 폴리에스터 복합재의 섬유 회수까지 가능합니다.</p>$q$,
  research_en = $q$<p>Charged macromolecules are everywhere, from biological macromolecules to the synthetic polyelectrolytes behind today’s leading technologies. Our group explores the physicochemical phenomena of charged macromolecules and translates them into soft, highly deformable functional devices.</p><p>Ionic Polymer Design and Synthesis<br>We synthesize polyelectrolytes and polymerized ionic liquids with controlled backbone chemistry, charge density, and counterion, then build them into elastomeric networks by chemical crosslinking, physical association, double networks, and polymerization-induced phase separation. Because the ions are tethered to the network, these materials stretch and conduct at the same time. We ask how crosslink density, ion content, and salt doping set the stiffness, the dielectric response, and the charge a material can store at an electrified interface.</p><p>Complex Coacervation and Phase Behavior<br>Mixing oppositely charged polyelectrolytes drives associative phase separation into a dense complex and a dilute supernatant. We map where those phase boundaries sit as a function of charge density, salt, and solvent, and connect them to the structure and mechanics of the dense phase. That dense phase is not simply a liquid. Water and salt plasticize it, so its glass transition can be tuned — and even driven electrically. A thermodynamic question becomes a handle on how fast ions move through the complex, and on how the complex behaves when it forms at an interface.</p><p>Soft Ionic Devices, Iontronics, and Electro-Adhesion<br>When a network of fixed anions meets a network of fixed cations, the mobile counterions rearrange into an ionic double layer at the junction. That layer responds to a few volts, so strong and reversible adhesion becomes possible at voltages a battery can supply. We study how the double layer forms and discharges, how network elasticity shapes its capacitance–voltage response, and how the same junctions rectify ionic current. We then build that behavior into devices: electro-adhesive clutches, grippers, and robotic end-effectors that switch stiffness and holding strength on demand.</p><p>Sustainable Polymer Chemistry<br>Most polymers are far easier to build than to take apart. We study depolymerization as a route to closed-loop chemical recycling, asking which linkages reopen under mild conditions and how a polymer's structure decides whether it comes back as clean monomer. Our catalysts are macroporous polyanion beads. Because the active sites are tethered to a solid support, the catalyst can be filtered out and used again, which makes continuous operation possible — including recovery of the fibers from polyester composites.</p>$q$
where name_ko = '김형준';

select name_ko, title_ko, keywords, length(bio_ko) bio_ko, length(bio_en) bio_en,
       length(research_ko) res_ko, length(research_en) res_en
from faculty where name_ko = '김형준';
